   - Creates a `BufferData` struct to store the results
   - Reads the header using `buffer.read(&result.header, sizeof(uint32_t))`
   - Resizes the vector to the expected data length
   - Reads the data into the vector using `buffer.read(result.data.data(), data_length)`

